---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ContactPerson } from "../components/ContactPerson";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>For contractors | Spokane List</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Free Spokane-area directory listings for contractors. Optional help with Google reviews, Business Profile, or a simple website."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">For contractors</p>
    <h1>Your listing is the point</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This directory is free. Homeowners use it to find a trade and share a clean
      profile in neighborhood chats and Facebook groups. You don’t need an
      account, and you don’t need to buy anything to stay listed.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What the free listing does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A shareable page with your name, trade, city, phone, and site.</li>
        <li>Google rating and review count when we have them.</li>
        <li>A listing link that holds up when someone pastes it in a group.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Keep your
        <a href="https://business.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >Google Business Profile</a
        >
        current, then <a href="/get-listed">request a listing</a> or a fix. We
        refresh from GBP—we don’t run a second profile you have to manage here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you ever want a hand</h2>
      <p>
        Some local contractors ask for help getting more Google reviews, cleaning
        up a Business Profile, or putting up a simple website that matches this
        listing. If that’s useful, you’re welcome to write. If not, the directory
        stays free either way.
      </p>
      <ContactPerson />
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/get-listed">Request a listing</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/">See the directory</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
